WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.035
-Our first guest is an Emmy an
Golden Globe-winning actress

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.337 size:81% position:41%
She directed and stars
in the film "Moxie,"

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.038 size:88% position:44% line:92%
which is on Netflix now.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
one of the all-time best,

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.943 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Amy Poehler. Hello, Amy!

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.745 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi, buddy!

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I'm going to
tell you this,

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is a true thing,
because I believe

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the third time we have
talked in this past year -

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
you keep looking
better and better on Zoom.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:23.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
Well, happy COVID-verssary

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:24.657 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Thank you very much.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every March 11th, me, you
Phoebe Bridgers,

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
let's get together,
let's talk about our year.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.164 line:92%
-I would like that, I think.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.866 size:75% position:38%
-I was just thinking
the other day that

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.534 line:92%
yours was the first show I did

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I started
doing press for "Moxie."

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:40.040
and now you're the last
piece of press I'm doing.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Full circle.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so usually,
this would be a junket

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you would
have to be out on the road

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.478 line:92%
talking about your movie.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have been talking
about it the same amount,

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.181 line:92%
but you have been at home.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you enjoyed
the home press tour?

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very much.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I know it's not as fun,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:57.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I cannot wait to be
back in your studio for sure

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to see everybody,
and to see you in person.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:03.296 size:81% position:41%
But, you know, one of
the misconceptions is,

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't really like people
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:10.170
-And so it's great, because
don't have to be around anybody.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And that's great.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.839 line:92%
-Well, I think that's why people

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
value being friends
with you so much,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:15.608 line:92%
is that from the outside,

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.910 size:84% position:42%
people assume you're
friends with everybody.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.579
but we have actually reall
made it through a gauntlet

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.681
to be at a place where you'r
willing to spend time with us.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can literally count on on
hand. I can count on one hand.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
How many people I like.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.254 line:92%
But you make that list, Seth

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You make that list.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know who else
is on that hand is

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:36.496 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Maya, Kenan, and Tina,

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you and Tina
hosted the Globes again.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Fourth time.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:44.370
And Maya and Kenan showed up
and what a delight they were

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:44.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What a delight.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it struck me,
I was confused, because,

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.443 size:75% position:38%
of course, Kenan did
"SNL" on Saturday,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:54.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then he was in
the L.A. half of the Globes.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For people that
have not seen the show,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
they played winners
of Least Original Song,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:04.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they came up, and Tina
had written this bit for them,

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in beautiful form,
Maya arrived already dressed

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and ready to party,

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:16.136
and Kenan had flown in right
from New York the evening before

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.238 line:92%
and had not yet read the sketch,

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were about
ready to go live.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those two are such geniuses,
they're like stunt men.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like when you se
a stunt man about to do a stun

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're kind of
joking around

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.948 line:92%
and they're really loose?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.782 line:92%
And they're just kind of like,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you're gonna
jump off this building?"

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.485 line:92%
"No, not if he pushes me first."

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just
so good at their jobs

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they were -- it was
awesome to have them around.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're the best.
-It should be noted,

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
it wasn't just reading lines
off a teleprompter.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.997 line:92%
There was also prop work.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
A fantastic joke is that
Maya reached under her dress

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.870 line:92%
and took off three high heels.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.672 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-She had three shoes.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.040 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And seamlessly did it.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, again,
you know me, terrible.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.546
You put a prop in a sketch
and then you basically jus

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
see me staring at it
the whole scene,

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.116
'cause I'm so nervous abou
what I'm going to have to do

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.719 size:75% position:38%
Whereas she, just so
gentle and perfect.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.855 line:92%
-Yeah, they're incredible.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.923 line:92%
And that night was so strange,

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know,
you're staring at an audienc

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.428 line:92%
that is separated and masked

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.364
and you can't really tell
when anybody's laughing,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.532 line:92%
because nobody laughs like -

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody laughs like you
think they're going to laugh

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:22.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know? Like --

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.237 line:92%
Everyone just laughs like --

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that's maybe
how their body moves.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:30.777 size:84% position:42%
So you can't tell if
maybe they tipping over

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
or if they're laughing,
you can't tell.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:36.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
So to be onstage with
that weird sci-fi quality

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
and with those two
was just a dream.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have been backstage at
Globes that you have hosted.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is both a really
fun energy backstage

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then there's the additiona
energy of the after party.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.562 size:75% position:38%
I'm assuming neither
of those happened.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.664 line:92%
-No food or drink was allowed.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.266 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No food or drink?

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Zero.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.803
-So what was backstage?
-I had to sneak in carrot sticks

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and my own water.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:01.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at one point,
I checked in with Tina on Zoom

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:02.642 line:92%
and she was eating something

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"What are you eating?"

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like,
"I'm eating sushi."

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Where did you get sushi?"

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.049 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So that was it.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
New York had sushi.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that, I think,
is the real...

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.455 size:84% position:42%
You were leaning into
the stereotype of L.A.,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
that all you had was
water and carrot sticks.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
we had tons of pills,

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:20.727 line:92%
and we all went for a hike

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.028 line:92%
-Oh, so pills were allowed

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:25.365 size:84% position:42%
-Of course pills were.
It's the Golden Globes.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.933 line:92%
Of course pills are allowed.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:30.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We'll be right back
with more from Amy Poehler

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.172
We're going to talk about
